### SKILL.md  [instructions]
- - ✅ **One-shot links** — token is invalidated after the first download
- - ✅ **Auto-cleanup** — file is deleted from `shared/` after download or expiry
- - ✅ **No login required** — anyone with the link can download once
- SHARE_PUBLIC_URL="https://share.yourdomain.com" node skills/share-onetime-link/scripts/server.js
- Or use the provided start script (edit `SHARE_PUBLIC_URL` first):
- # Copies file to shared/, returns a public link valid for 30 minutes
- The agent will:
- 1. Copy the file to `shared/`
- 2. Call `POST /generate` on the local server
- 3. Return the public link with expiry info
- curl http://localhost:5050/status
- ## How it works
- 1. `share-file.js` copies the file to `shared/` and calls `POST /generate`
- 2. The server generates a random 64-char hex token and stores `{ filename, filePath, expiresAt }`
- 3. On `GET /dl/:token`: validates token, streams the file, marks as downloaded, deletes file + token
- 4. A cleanup interval runs every 60s to remove expired tokens and files
- | Variable | Default | Description |
- |----------|---------|-------------|
- | `SHARE_PUBLIC_URL` | `http://localhost:5050` | Public base URL for generated links |
- | `SHARE_PORT` | `5050` | Local server port |
- | `SHARED_DIR` | `workspace/shared/` | Directory for shared files |
- - Links are single-use: once downloaded, the token is immediately invalidated
- - No directory listing — only direct token access works
+ - ✅ **One-shot links** — token invalidated after first download
+ - ✅ **Auto-cleanup** — file deleted from `shared/` after download or expiry
+ - ✅ **Protected endpoints** — `/generate` and `/status` require `SHARE_SECRET`
+ - ✅ **No login required for download** — anyone with the link can download once
+ - Set `SHARE_SECRET` to a strong random string (recommended)
+ SHARE_PUBLIC_URL="https://share.yourdomain.com" \
+ SHARE_SECRET="your-strong-random-secret" \
+ node skills/share-onetime-link/scripts/server.js
+ Or use `start.sh` (edit variables first):
+ SHARE_SECRET="your-secret" \
+ # Returns a public link valid for 30 minutes
+ curl -H "x-share-secret: your-secret" http://localhost:5050/status
+ | Variable | Required | Default | Description |
+ |----------|----------|---------|-------------|
+ | `SHARE_PUBLIC_URL` | **Yes** | `http://localhost:5050` | Public base URL for generated links |
+ | `SHARE_SECRET` | Recommended | *(none)* | Secret key for `/generate` and `/status` endpoints |
+ | `SHARE_PORT` | No | `5050` | Local server port |
+ | `SHARED_DIR` | No | `workspace/shared/` | Directory for shared files |
+ - `/dl/:token` is **public by design** — anyone with the link can download once
+ - `/generate` and `/status` are **protected by `SHARE_SECRET`** — set it before exposing publicly
+ - If `SHARE_SECRET` is not set, a warning is logged and endpoints are unprotected
+ - Never put sensitive files in `SHARED_DIR` unless you intend to share them

